<!--
    GHOST. A sheet ghost: domed head, three-lobe wavy hem, two eyes and a mouth.

    THE EYES AND MOUTH ARE HOLES CUT BY WINDING DIRECTION, not by
    android:fillType="evenOdd". fillType needs API 24 and this app's minSdk is
    21, where it is silently ignored — which would fill the face solid and leave
    a featureless blob on old devices only, never reproducing in testing. The
    body is wound clockwise (it leaves the top heading RIGHT) and each facial
    feature the other way (arc sweep-flag 0), so the default nonZero rule cuts
    them on every API.

    I got that backwards on the first build and shipped a faceless blob: with y
    pointing down, sweep-flag 1 draws CLOCKWISE on screen, the same direction as
    the body, so the features ADDED winding instead of cancelling it.

    THE FIRST VERSION WAS ALSO LOPSIDED AND TOO SMALL. Its dome ran x=6..20 —
    centre 13, not 12 — so the ghost sat half a unit right of centre inside its
    own viewport, and it filled only 58% of the 24-unit box while the snowflake
    beside it filled 72%. Rendered at the same button size, the ghost simply
    looked smaller. Now symmetric about x=12 and 17.6 units wide, measured from
    a screenshot rather than judged by eye.

    The figure starts at y=2.2 rather than the rounder 1.8 so that its INK is
    centred on y=12, not its bounding box. A ghost is top-heavy — solid dome,
    scalloped hem — and at 1.8 it measured 4.5px high in a 183px button.
-->
